  "_readme": "STARTER SET, not yet reviewed by a native speaker. Bands are graded by GraphemeCounter (java.text.BreakIterator), same rule as the English file -- but Java's BreakIterator does NOT merge Khmer coeng (subscript consonant) sequences into one grapheme the way some other Unicode libraries do, so counts run higher than they look. Verified against the actual game code: tiny<=2, short=3, medium=4, long=5-6, epic=7-8. tricky and lore are thematic, not length-gated, same as the English file. A word lives in exactly one pool. IMPORTANT: EnemyType's minWordLength/maxWordLength windows were tuned against the English bands -- they will rarely get an exact match against these Khmer bands and will lean on WordBank's closest-length fallback instead. That's not a bug (the fallback exists for this), but pacing/difficulty-feel should be re-tuned per language before shipping Khmer.",
